 "rules": [
  {
   "section": "Design rules 9.5",
   "text": "**Notice** — Neutral / warning / error (L5); stays until the cause is gone. **Warning** when something blocks the main action or runs on a timer (offline, locks, near expiry); **error** when an action failed; **neutral** only for side information (D-54). Text wraps balanced. **Placement:** a notice that is the **result of an action** sits next to the control that did it — on a screen with a pinned bar, inside the bar above its button, in the band style of §3 (Home \"ending soon\", setup / add / request failures, the offer's \"Couldn't turn on…\", the case and calling bar notices); on a screen without a bar, 16 below the field it came from (D-98) or 8 below the button. A notice about **the bar's own action** — the result of the last tap, or why its button is disabled now (offline, \"No cases right now\") — is also in the bar. A notice about the **screen's general situation** (unlock \"isn't available\", Home idle-expired, manually ended, expired-pending, stop-pending) stays at the top of the panel, not tied to a button. **Alignment (D-86, 2026-11-03):** the band inside the bar is centred (icon and text as a group, wrapped lines centred, balanced breaks kept); every other notice (top of page, inside sheets, in content) stays left-aligned."
  },
  {
   "section": "Design rules L5",
   "text": "L5 — Notice text (`.tm-notice`): 14/20."
  },
  {
   "section": "Design rules 9.5",
   "text": "**Rule** — One message per cause — never field error + notice + toast for the same thing."
  }
 ],
